    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d468">

                <pb facs="0523" n="511" sameAs="frus:frus1937v01/pg511"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.1121 Fernandez, Antonio/32: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Consul at Seville</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Bay</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-06-05T14:00:00-04:00">June 5, 1937—2 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Antonio Fernandez Villa, American citizen, reported imprisoned and about to be
                    tried at Palma de Mallorca. As we have no consular representative in Palma
                    please request insurgent authorities to postpone any action in this case until
                    we are able to send a consular officer to Palma to investigate and report.</p>
                <pb facs="0524" n="512" xml:id="pg512"/>
                <p>As there is no possibility of communication between Barcelona and Palma at this
                    time we are endeavoring to make arrangements to send one of our officers from
                    Marseille or Genoa.<anchor n="70" xml:id="d468-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d468-f1" n="70" xml:id="d468-f1-content">
                <p>T. Monroe Fisher, Vice Consul at Leghorn, was sent to Palma de Mallorca to
                    investigate and report.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
